Quality is foundational to circular economy value creation—products perceived as high-quality are more likely to be valued, maintained, repaired, and recovered at end-of-life. Quality encompasses functional reliability, aesthetic durability, and experience consistency across use cycles. Paradoxically, quality often enables lower material consumption by reducing need for replacement and enabling efficient sharing and reuse systems. Design for quality requires intentional material selection, manufacturing precision, sensory excellence, and performance testing that communicates confidence in longevity.